{title: Redeem Us}
{subtitle: Psalms 44:27}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Bb6] | [Bb6] | [D7] |
| [Gm] | [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb6]Awake Lord why do [D7]you [Gm]sleep
Rouse your[Ebmaj7]self from your [Bb6]rest
Do not reject us [D7]forever
[Gm]Keep us in your sight [Ebmaj7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb6]Why hide your face a[D7]way
[Gm]Forget our deep [Ebmaj7]distress
[Bb6]Our soul is sunk [D7]to dust
Our [Gm]body [F]clings to [Ebmaj7]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Rise up and [Bb]help us [D7]now
Redeem us in your [Gm]love
[Eb]Steadfast [Bb]kindness holds us [D7]fast
When all our strength is [Gm]gone
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ebmaj7]Rise up and [Bb]help us [D7]now
Redeem us in your [Gm]love
[Eb]Steadfast [Bb]kindness holds us [D7]fast
When all our strength is [Gm]gone
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Gm] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] | [D7] | ×2
| [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ebmaj7]Rise up and [Bb]help us
[D7]Redeem us for your [Gm]love [Ebmaj7][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
